# Fallback only — NOT the primary pruning mechanism.
#
# Finding: when package.json `files` lists a directory (e.g. "sidecar/"), npm
# includes that directory wholesale and does NOT re-apply .npmignore to its
# contents. So the actual pruning of sidecar/tests, __pycache__, *.pyc, etc. is
# done by negated globs in package.json `files` ("!sidecar/tests/**", …) — see
# there. This file only takes effect if `files` ever stops using directory
# entries; it's kept as belt-and-suspenders. Patterns use .gitignore semantics.

# Python tests bundled under the shipped sidecar/ server
tests/

# Python build / venv / cache cruft (untracked, present on dev machines)
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.venv/
.pytest_cache/
.python-version

# Local, gitignored runtime config (never published)
litellm_config.yaml

# Editor / OS / build cruft
.DS_Store
*.map
dist/
